;; repr/ocaml's read level's divergences (bin/reap's OCaml read cell; doc/ocaml/OCAML-SURVEY.md, "As built: O8 (write-ahead)"):
;; the classes every file of test/ocaml/read-results.edn that does not pass falls into, in test/goi/divergences.edn's format,
;; matched against "RESULT REASON" as the record writes them (REASON "CLASS KIND: MESSAGE", the class bin/repr-ocaml roundtrip
;; gives a file the oracle rejects, test/ocaml/roundtrip-known.edn's). The oracle is ocamlc 5.5.0's own parser (tools/ocdump on
;; compiler-libs): a file it rejects is the corpus's, judged on the oracle's message (survey §5.4), not a read failure of Arbace's.
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :oracle-rejects
  :title "files ocamlc's parser rejects: the testsuite's parse-error and lexer tests, build scripts and preprocessor input"
  :kind :design
  :why "the testsuite's parse-errors, lexing and messages tests are deliberately invalid OCaml (their expected output is the error); the opam set's pkg/pkg.ml, build.ml and toplevel init files use topfind directives, yojson's files cppo's: none is OCaml ocamlc accepts. The read level reads what the oracle reads; each rejection is recorded with ocamlc's message (roundtrip-known.edn), which the round trip checks unchanged"
  :decided "survey §5.4; O2, O7 (\"As built\": the helper's rejections classed)"
  :match [#"^reject (syntax-error|lexer-error) (syntax|lexer): "]}
 {:id :templates
  :title "the stdlib's macro templates"
  :kind :design
  :why "stdlib/templates/*.template.mli are inputs to the stdlib's build (sed templates for Float and MoreLabels), not OCaml"
  :decided "O1 (test/ocaml/corpora.edn's :ocdump-rejects)"
  :match [#"^reject template syntax: "]}]
